<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Dubs Performance Analyzer profiling tab for Animal Food Preference.
  Adds an "AnimalFoodPreference" tab to the Analyzer with the mod's hot paths
  pre-wired so they can be profiled directly. Only active when Dubs Performance
  Analyzer is installed; harmless otherwise.

  ====================================================================
  HARD RULES (Dubs Performance Analyzer parses this with DynamicTypeBuilder;
  violating these crashes Analyzer init, not just this tab):

  1. NO comments or stray text as DIRECT children of <Analyzer>.
     XmlParser.Parse iterates every child node of <Analyzer> and calls
     CreateType(node.Name, ...) without skipping XmlComment nodes. A comment's
     node.Name is "#comment", stripped to "comment" — so two top-level comments
     both DefineType("comment") => "Duplicate type name within an assembly" crash
     at DynamicTypeBuilder.CreateType. Keep ALL commentary up here, above the
     root element (a comment before <Analyzer> is not a child of it — safe).

  2. Tab names are reduced to LETTERS ONLY before becoming a type
     (string.Concat over char.IsLetter). "AnimalFoodPreference" is already
     letters-only and unique, so it is safe.

  3. <Types> already profiles every method on a type. Do NOT also list that
     same type's methods under <Methods> on the same tab — redundant double-add.
     (Below, <Methods> lists only the patched VANILLA host methods, not our patch
     types — no overlap.)

  4. The parser looks for Analyzer.xml. Keep it capitalized "Analyzer.xml".

  5. Dev-only file — git-ignored so it is not committed/shipped to Steam.

  Element guide (method syntax is Namespace.Type:Method — return/args inferred):
    <Types>    profile every method on the listed type
    <Methods>  profile a single method (used here for the patched host methods)

  Docs: https://github.com/Dubwise56/Dubs-Performance-Analyzer#using-the-analyzerxml
-->
<Analyzer>
    <AnimalFoodPreference>
        <Types>
            <li>AnimalFoodPreference.BestFoodSourceOnMap_Patch</li>
            <li>AnimalFoodPreference.FoodOptimality_Patch</li>
            <li>AnimalFoodPreference.FoodClassifier</li>
        </Types>
        <Methods>
            <li>RimWorld.FoodUtility:BestFoodSourceOnMap</li>
            <li>RimWorld.FoodUtility:FoodOptimality</li>
        </Methods>
    </AnimalFoodPreference>
</Analyzer>
